# Models

This project uses **Grok 4.7** (plus Composer 2.5 for ops). Effort is encoded in the Cursor Task `model` slug. Bracket overlay strings (`grok-4.7[effort=…,fast=false]`) are **not** valid Task models — Cursor’s allowlist does not accept them.

## Allowed Task models (Cursor allowlist slugs)

| Class | `model` string | Use when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Complex / greenfield / scroll motor / architecture | `cursor-grok-4.7-high` | Default for complex work; first anime.js path, Canvas UI integration, ambiguous UX |
| Follow-up / polish / light work | `cursor-grok-4.7-medium` | Polish, wiring, bounded tweaks; also when the human says `low` (no `*-low` slug exists) |
| Ops | `composer-2.5` | Commits, shell, move/copy, mechanical deploy — only these |

**Only these three.** No other Grok major (4.6 / 4.5), no xhigh, no Fast variants.

## Effort shorthand from the human

Bare effort words map to the matching slug above:

| Human says | Task `model` |
| --- | --- |
| `high` | `cursor-grok-4.7-high` |
| `medium` | `cursor-grok-4.7-medium` |
| `low` | `cursor-grok-4.7-medium` (no `cursor-grok-4.7-low` — do not invent it) |
| `xhigh` / Extra High | **Refuse.** Ask for `high` or `medium`. Do **not** launch xhigh. |

Confirm the mapped slug in one short line. Never leave Task `model` empty because they typed a bare effort word.

## Never Fast (blocking)

- **Never** Fast for parent chat, Agent, Plan, Ask, Debug, Multitask, or Tasks.
- Forbidden UI / slug forms include: `Grok 4.7 High Fast`, `Grok 4.6 High Fast`, `* Fast`, `composer-2.5-fast`, any `*-fast` / `*Fast*` product label.
- If the Cursor UI only offers a Fast variant of an otherwise-allowed model: **stop and tell the human** — do not pick Fast.

## Independence from the model picker (blocking)

Subagent Tasks are **totally independent** of whatever is selected (or empty) in the Cursor model picker.

- Every Task **launch and resume** **must** pass an explicit `model` string from the table above.
- **Never** `inherit`, Auto, default, or omit `model` hoping the picker / parent chat fills it in.
- An empty or unset picker must **not** change which model a subagent gets.
- Prefer the parent chat itself on **Grok 4.7 High** or **Grok 4.7 Medium** (non-Fast). That choice still **never** flows into Task `model` via inherit.

Refuse launch/resume if `model` is missing, `inherit`, or not in the allowlist. Do not invent a substitute family.

## Cursor allowlist drift (blocking)

1. **Read the live Cursor Task allowlist** for this session before launch.
2. Take the **intersection** with this project’s allowed table (`cursor-grok-4.7-high`, `cursor-grok-4.7-medium`, `composer-2.5`).
3. If the intersection is **empty** (session only exposes 4.6 / xhigh / Fast / inherit among candidates): **stop and tell the human**. Do **not** substitute `cursor-grok-4.6-*`, xhigh, Fast, or `inherit`.

## If Cursor rejects a slug

Stop and report which slug was rejected. **Do not** fall back to `inherit`, `cursor-grok-4.6-*`, `composer-2.5-fast`, xhigh, or any other family. Prefer `cursor-grok-4.7-high` as the default for complex work when choosing among allowed slugs that are also in the live allowlist.

## Poteto / Gentle conflict (project wins)

If poteto (or Gentle) teaches role `inherit-parent` / `auto` → omit Task `model` so the subagent inherits the parent chat model: **ignore that for this project**. Project overlay wins — always pass an explicit allowlisted slug. Never omit `model` on launch or resume.

## Never

- `inherit` on any Task (writers **and** explorers/reviewers)
- Any **Fast** model (parent or Task), including `composer-2.5-fast` and UI “High Fast” / “Medium Fast”
- `*xhigh*` — even if Cursor lists it
- Bracket forms as Task `model` (`grok-4.7[effort=…]`, `composer-2.5[fast=false]`)
- `cursor-grok-4.6-*`, `grok-4.6-*`, `cursor-grok-4.5-*`, gemini, muse
- Inventing `cursor-grok-4.7-low` or any slug not in the table
- Putting effort in the prompt (`EFFORT:`) instead of the `model` slug
- Substituting 4.6 or Fast if the allowlist rejects 4.7 high/medium — stop and report
- Relying on parent-chat or picker state for subagent model selection
- Omitting `model` on resume
